            {
                "entry_id": "147ed526-66f2-37a3-b687-12ba93d38b1a",
                "word": "blandices",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "f0aca5c6-1051-4025-a41a-3ceb6e590d0f",
                        "entry_id": "147ed526-66f2-37a3-b687-12ba93d38b1a",
                        "tags": [
                            "singular"
                        ],
                        "form": "blandice"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b1c73125-fcc5-386a-8c5c-a78fa8ba44b0",
                        "entry_id": "147ed526-66f2-37a3-b687-12ba93d38b1a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Flatteries artificieuses, caresses, ce qui charme et séduit."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "191f42b5-6106-4e45-8faf-ee4043b41ff2",
                                "sense_id": "b1c73125-fcc5-386a-8c5c-a78fa8ba44b0",
                                "text": "… il ne pouvait résister aux incantations, aux charmes et aux blandices des filles galantes, qu’il rencontrait par essaims, dans l’ombre, […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "924f60ce-0060-4af2-9154-27774e6a5db6",
                                "sense_id": "b1c73125-fcc5-386a-8c5c-a78fa8ba44b0",
                                "text": "Un moine, si j'étais chrétien, ne m’enverrait pas autrement dans le siècle, ne m’exhorterait pas avec plus de zèle à défendre contre les blandices de l'esprit mondain le soin de mon salut et du Royaume de Dieu."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0929bf0a-539f-4271-abac-a51ddf666fb0",
                                "sense_id": "b1c73125-fcc5-386a-8c5c-a78fa8ba44b0",
                                "text": "L’amitié ou l’aversion comptaient d’ailleurs finalement aussi peu que les blandices charnelles."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e576f40e-9e44-46a0-a480-9cb7b8cd4b1c",
                                "sense_id": "b1c73125-fcc5-386a-8c5c-a78fa8ba44b0",
                                "text": "La pénétration n’était pas la qualité la plus développée de mon esprit ; alors que je partais, elle me gratifia d’un de ses habituels sourires, comme si je l’avais nourrie ce jour-là de toutes les blandices de l’amour."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fdb921bc-810a-4edc-af6b-61c0e3c5c9c8",
                                "sense_id": "b1c73125-fcc5-386a-8c5c-a78fa8ba44b0",
                                "text": "Ne pouvant se fonder que sur les formes apparentes des mots et sur leur sens tels que les suggérait l’intuition, tous [les philologues] étaient nécessairement exposés aux aimables blandices de la spéculation."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2dbf0499-a3ec-4384-aa2f-69d79d14f718",
                        "source_entry_id": "147ed526-66f2-37a3-b687-12ba93d38b1a",
                        "source_sense_id": "b1c73125-fcc5-386a-8c5c-a78fa8ba44b0",
                        "target_lang_word": "blandishment",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "blandishment",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f2ef6aa7-fb56-3c47-bc6b-296d519be7a8",
                                        "entry_id": "19d23c22-50a7-3c87-9d2d-6a2d0db31f24",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Often in the plural form blandishments: a flattering speech or action designed to influence or persuade."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a74cb537-e38f-49ed-83dc-484a8924aa04",
                                                "sense_id": "f2ef6aa7-fb56-3c47-bc6b-296d519be7a8",
                                                "text": "Thus Her with Indignation frowning, ſtern, / With Tears, and Blandiſhments Æneas ſooth’d : / She bends here Eyes averſe upon the Ground ; / And by his Speech begun is mov’d no more, / Than a hard Flint, or fix’d Marpeſian Rock."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "15fc86ee-97f3-45cb-8f42-7485e6d1ba2a",
                                                "sense_id": "f2ef6aa7-fb56-3c47-bc6b-296d519be7a8",
                                                "text": "She looked up as she heard his footsteps, and the gracious smile which her lips put on, was an invitation to make himself happy in a seat beside her. But he resisted the blandishment, and lifting his hat as he passed, with a smile in return, he soon disappeared from her presence, and joined the two who awaited him."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1387a531-cae5-4ab0-a122-d599e7fd965d",
                                                "sense_id": "f2ef6aa7-fb56-3c47-bc6b-296d519be7a8",
                                                "text": "Pat found subject and scene of his wooing unaltered, but all his specious blandishments could not induce the matured matron of 'Gi' Away Nothin' 'All' to join fortunes, though his perseverance would have delighted Bruce's spider."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1cb227f8-057c-3134-b21c-746d32dbab32",
                                        "entry_id": "19d23c22-50a7-3c87-9d2d-6a2d0db31f24",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something alluring or attractive."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "66130f40-0c9d-4a3e-8d9d-a3f4fb5b2a2a",
                                                "sense_id": "1cb227f8-057c-3134-b21c-746d32dbab32",
                                                "text": "We need intellectual leaders who are prepared to resist the blandishments of power and influence and who are willing to work for an ideal, however small may be the prospects of its early realization."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "78aa601d-b39d-3d85-9657-2281b9f1a13c",
                                        "entry_id": "19d23c22-50a7-3c87-9d2d-6a2d0db31f24",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Allurement, attraction."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
